{"shortDescription":"China's fuel oil exports, mainly for marine fuel bunkering, fell in October after a strong September, while fuel oil imports rebounded, customs data showed on Friday.October export volumes totalled 1.62 million metric tons, or about 333,000 barrels a day, down 37% from September but up 32% from the…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["China's fuel oil exports, mainly for marine fuel bunkering, fell in October after a strong September, while fuel oil imports rebounded, customs data showed on Friday."]},{"type":"p","children":["October export volumes totalled 1.62 million metric tons, or about 333,000 barrels a day, down 37% from September but up 32% from the same month a year ago, according to General Administration of Customs data."]},{"type":"p","children":["Bunker export activity slowed in October with more vessels calling at regional Asian hub Singapore, which offered lower prices during most of October for the mainstay low-sulphur fuel grade than Zhoushan and Shanghai ports, market sources said."]},{"type":"p","children":["Meanwhile, fuel oil imports into China, which typically head to refineries and the marine fuel blending pool, recovered to a seven-month high in October as feedstock demand improved."]},{"type":"p","children":["Customs data showed imports totaled 1.95 million tons for October, up 72% from September and 4% higher than a year earlier."]},{"type":"p","children":["The table below shows China's fuel oil exports and imports in metric tons. The export section largely captures low-sulphur bunkering sales along China's coast."]},{"type":"p","children":["The import volumes include purchases under ordinary trade subject to import duties and consumption taxes, as well as imports into bonded storage."]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Exports (2026)"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell",